  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(a) Concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math> is performed by leaching with dilute&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi></math> solution<br />(b) Pig iron is formed in blast furnace<br />(c) Blister Cu is produced in Bessemer converter<br />(d) Froth floatation method is used for sulphide<br />ores.</p><p>Note : During extraction of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math>&nbsp;reverberatory furnace is involved.</p>"
